.TH NN 1 "2026" "nn 0.1.0" "NN Manual"
.SH NAME
nn \- neural-network engineering toolkit
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nn
[\fIglobal options\fR]
.I command
[\fIargs\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Inspect, analyze, compare, and (optionally) execute neural-network artifacts from the command line.
One native executable, subcommands, no GUI. Execution is an optional convenience via linked runtimes
(ONNX Runtime, LiteRT); inspection does not require a runtime.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show help.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Increase verbosity.
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Quiet mode.
.TP
.B \-\-json
JSON output (schema_version 1 where applicable).
.TP
.B \-\-yaml
YAML output.
.TP
.B \-\-porcelain
Stable machine-readable text (tab-separated key/value).
.TP
.B \-\-threads \fIN\fR
Thread hint for runtimes that honor it.
.SH COMMANDS
inspect, ops, tensors, io, metadata, hash, diff, graph, memory, compute, quant, sparsity, lint,
run, compare, test, validate, regression, benchmark, profile, compat, target, partition,
convert, optimize, extract, canonicalize, bisect, doctor, formats, backends, targets, config, help, version.
.SH SEE ALSO
nn-inspect(1), nn-run(1), nn-compare(1), nn-diff(1), nn-sparsity(1), nn-target(1),
nn-formats(1), nn-doctor(1)
